    {
      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>A home rarely fails on one big thing. It slips on small things that lapsed between visits: a late supervision, a gap in the fire door log, a safeguarding action nobody closed. One monthly round catches them.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>A monthly round pulls the recurring care audits into one check.</li><li>It covers safety and environment, people and records, medication and a mock inspection.</li><li>We found no single legal format for a monthly audit. Your policies and risk assessments set it.</li><li>Quickler runs the round in WhatsApp. It is not a care records system.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "Safety and environment",
      "heading": "The safety checks",
      "html": "<p>Walk the building. Falls hazards and moving and handling. Hoists and slings under LOLER, which HSE says need a thorough examination at least every six months where they lift people, unless a written examination scheme sets another interval. Fire and legionella controls. Infection prevention. Check each against the home's own risk assessments.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "People and records",
      "heading": "Safeguarding, training and care plans",
      "html": "<p>Are safeguarding referrals logged and actions closed? Are training and supervision dates current? Does a sample of care plans match the resident today?</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "Readiness",
      "heading": "Medication, incidents and the mock inspection",
      "html": "<p>Medication: storage temperatures, controlled drugs records and administration checks. See the <a href=\"/pages/medication-storage-audit-care-uk.html\">medication storage audit</a>. Incidents: look back at accidents and what was done. Then a mock inspection against your regulator's framework.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "Sources",
      "heading": "Official sources",
      "html": "<p>The six-monthly thorough examination for hoists, slings and other equipment that lifts people comes from HSE guidance on LOLER (regulation 9), which also says a written examination scheme can set different intervals; the care home guidance HSG220 lists hoists and slings as covered. We found no law that sets a monthly audit format, so the page says so and leaves frequency to your own policies and risk assessments. The regulators are the Care Quality Commission (England), the Care Inspectorate (Scotland), Care Inspectorate Wales and RQIA (Northern Ireland). LOLER and the health and safety law apply in Great Britain, and Northern Ireland has its own. Fire, legionella, infection control and medication requirements were not checked on this page. Official sources checked on 18 November 2026.</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.hse.gov.uk/work-equipment-machinery/lift-persons.htm\" rel=\"noopener\">Lifting equipment used for lifting people at work (HSE)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://books.hse.gov.uk/gempdf/hsg220.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\">Health and safety in care homes, HSG220 (HSE)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/1998/2307/regulation/9\" rel=\"noopener\">LOLER 1998 regulation 9 (legislation.gov.uk)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.cqc.org.uk/\" rel=\"noopener\">Care Quality Commission (England)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.careinspectorate.scot/\" rel=\"noopener\">Care Inspectorate (Scotland)</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.careinspectorate.wales/\" rel=\"noopener\">Care Inspectorate Wales</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.rqia.org.uk/\" rel=\"noopener\">RQIA (Northern Ireland)</a></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "faq",
      "heading": "Questions",
      "html": "<h3>What goes in a monthly care home compliance checklist?</h3><p>Health and safety and the environment (falls, hoists under LOLER, fire, legionella), infection control, safeguarding, training and supervision, care plans, medication, and a mock inspection.</p><h3>Is a monthly audit a legal requirement?</h3><p>We found no single legal monthly format. Your own policies and risk assessments set how often. Keep records so you can show the checks were done.</p><h3>Does the checklist change by UK nation?</h3><p>The safety checks are much the same. The framework differs. CQC covers England, the Care Inspectorate covers Scotland, Care Inspectorate Wales covers Wales and RQIA covers Northern Ireland.</p><h3>Can I run the round on WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. You get each prompt in WhatsApp and reply by text, voice note or photo. No new app to install.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/care-home-audit-software-uk.html\">Care home audit software</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/cqc-compliance-audit-checklist-uk.html\">CQC compliance audit checklist</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/safeguarding-audit-care-home-uk.html\">Safeguarding audit for care homes</a></li></ul>"
